Validated facts and confirmed findings
- Rule E3006 (ResourceType) validates CloudFormation resource types against provider schemas per region.
  - File: src/cfnlint/rules/resources/ResourceType.py
  - Logic iterates validator.context.regions and checks:
    - If a resource has a Condition, it uses cfn.conditions.build_scenerios_on_region(condition_name, region) to determine if the condition can be true in that region.
    - It validates that the resource type exists for that region via PROVIDER_SCHEMA_MANAGER.get_resource_types(region=region).
    - It skips validation for Custom::, AWS::Serverless::, and ::MODULE types.
- Conditions and region handling are implemented by:
  - src/cfnlint/conditions/conditions.py (class Conditions)
    - build_scenerios_on_region(name, region) yields True/False possibilities depending on whether the named condition compares Ref: AWS::Region to a specific region string (via EqualParameter and Equal.is_region).
  - src/cfnlint/conditions/_equals.py (EqualParameter, Equal)
    - Recognizes region comparisons using REF_REGION and returns is_region tuple (True, region) when appropriate.
- Unit tests for ResourceType condition behavior exist and set expectations:
  - test/unit/rules/resources/test_type.py
    - When build_scenerios_on_region returns [True], ResourceType should emit a ValidationError for a non-existent type in that region.
    - When it returns [False], ResourceType should produce no error for that region/resource.
- Running the test suite produced 3 failing integration tests both before and after the ResourceType change:
